        "ballot_id": "B003",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "For the development of optical lattice clocks, enabling extraordinary advances in precision timekeeping and new tests of fundamental physics."
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B024",
    "B039"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "Optical lattice clocks are a durable advance in measurement: they have been independently demonstrated, steadily improved, and used both for precision timekeeping and tests of fundamental physics. Katori and Ye made complementary contributions to establishing the approach. The result has a clearly identifiable experimental achievement and a maturity that supports judging its lasting value.",
    "case_against": "The prize scope must distinguish the foundational clock work from the broader history of optical frequency metrology and later technical advances. The case also depends on weighing fundamental scientific reach alongside exceptional performance and practical value.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson argues that Katori and Ye made central, complementary contributions and that the clocks' repeated demonstrations and scientific uses make the achievement both foundational and broadly enabling.",
        "response": "I agree that the two-person attribution and long experimental record are strong. I would keep the citation focused on optical lattice clocks, so the award recognizes their specific advance without claiming the whole history of optical frequency metrology."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson places the Higgs discovery first, citing its confirmation of a central Standard Model prediction, independent experimental results, and more than a decade of follow-up.",
        "response": "The discovery's scientific importance and maturity are compelling. The difficulty is assigning a few individual laureates to work by two very large collaborations. Optical lattice clocks offer a more bounded attribution while still recognizing a consequential experimental achievement."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "The historical boundary between the original optical lattice clock contributions and later enabling advances needs careful review.",
      "The lasting scientific impact of the clocks beyond their technical performance and metrological applications should be weighed."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
